beetroot on vegan yaki with crispy olive  crumble grilled leek with horseradish  and black sesame seed these vegetarian  dishes were created by Stefan Henshaw  head chef at the Berlin restaurant  cookies cream since 2007 the restaurants  just been awarded a Michelin star for us  it felt great because we hadn't been  expecting it we had been working towards  this for 10 years we are who we are  we try to be authentic we cook with love  and good ingredients this is a great  honor not just for me but for the entire  team chef Anne Henshall prepares his  vegetarian dishes with a team of six and  he does it without resorting to classic  meat substitutes like tofu or seitan  vegetables herbs and lettuce are all he  needs for his edible creations and  Stefan Henschel himself isn't even a  vegetarian it doesn't bother me to limit  my cooking to vegetables because I think  vegetarian cuisines more multifaceted  and colorful there are so many different  possibilities herbs just the colors of  beets for example red yellow he takes a  break on the restaurants roof chef Anne  grew up in the Eastern German state of  Saxony there he trained as a chef in  north rhine-westphalia in western  germany in 2001 he moved to Berlin and  learn to cook gourmet quality in the  two-star restaurant Fasil among others  then he started at cookies cream this is  a good place to reset yourself when  you're burned out or stressed in the  summer I tell my team when you eat you  don't have to sit at a table downstairs  you can go out on the roof when the sun  shining which goes of stuff bye ladies  don't know when they're coming out from  I do happen  a note delivers the herb some vegetables  for the restaurant weekly straight from  his own fields at the Brandenburg farmer  specializes in rare vegetables such as  Malabar spinach or Paris market carrots  they're known to be especially flavorful  he's been working with chef on Henschel  for many years the nice thing about  Paige's produce is that it's about taste  color and shape you can see that in the  vegetables the kitchen prepares so well  for me when preparing his vegetable  creations the chef's can even draw upon  his years of experience making meat  dishes after salting the beets he  wrapped them in tin foil and banks them  in the oven for 35 minutes at 160  degrees Celsius preserves the complete  flavor it's like when you braise a roast  you don't boil out the flavor the pure  taste has to remain in the vegetable the  vegetarian cuisine is more complex than  meat dishes because every individual  vegetable has to go through several  stages of preparation to ensure it'll  turn out especially tasty but the great  challenge for vegetarian cuisine is in  the restaurant of our guests eat meat  and we have to satisfy them as well  our dishes aren't necessarily light just  because they're vegetarian they can be  very rich cookies cream is one of the  trendiest restaurants in downtown Berlin  its patrons have included American actor  Tom Hanks and celebrity chef Jamie  Oliver as is often the case with the  cities in spots the entrance is in a  courtyard it serves about 120 guests  daily  Stefan Angela the dishes taste fantastic  because it doesn't just take the  standard dishes and leave out the meat  and substitute it with something else  he conjures up entirely new dishes  complete no good at all everything you  tasted quite unique you can certainly do  without the meat and we really enjoy it  here the cookies creme kitchen even  experiments with vegetables in desserts  this is bluebird sherbet with celery  rain is definitely to carry on the way  that we are but at the same time to keep  developing what we've achieved so far  and keep growing together as a team for  Stefan Henschel and his vegetarian  dishes a second mission a star may be on  the horizon
 

